Temperature Conversion Program in C

A simple and interactive C program that converts temperatures between Celsius (°C) and Fahrenheit (°F).

What I Learned

Through this project, I explored some important C programming concepts:

Variables & Data Types – Using char and float to store different types of data.
User Input & Output – Using scanf() and printf() to interact with users.
Conditional Statements – Implementing if, else if, and else.
Logical Operators – Using || (OR) to handle uppercase and lowercase choices.
Mathematical Operations – Applying temperature conversion formulas.
Input Validation – Handling invalid user choices with error messages.
Formatted Output – Using %.1f to display temperatures with one decimal place.
Menu-Driven Programming – Creating an interactive program with multiple options.

Conversion	Formula
Celsius to Fahrenheit	(C × 9/5) + 32
Fahrenheit to Celsius	(F − 32) × 5/9


My Takeaway

This project helped me understand how to combine user input, conditional logic, and mathematical operations to build an interactive program.

Every small project is another step towards becoming a better programmer!
